From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Dec 2025 20:38:32 +0530
Subject: feat: add canvas noise per renderer support

This patch enables custom canvas noise seed support per WebContents in Electron.
It allows Electron apps to control canvas fingerprinting by passing canvasSeed
via additionalArguments in webPreferences, providing deterministic canvas noise
for fingerprinting protection.

Changes:
- Restored canvas noise infrastructure files that were deleted from Chromium
- Added ShouldEnableCanvasNoise() method to ChromeContentBrowserClient that
  always returns true, bypassing profile and tracking protection checks
- Enabled kCanvasNoise feature by default in interventions_features.cc
- Modified CanvasNoiseTokenData::GetBrowserToken() to support custom seeds:
  - First checks BrowserContext for stored canvas seed
  - Falls back to parsing canvasSeed from command line arguments
  - Supports double precision seeds converted to uint64_t
  - Generates random token if no seed provided
- Added SetCanvasSeed() method to allow Electron to set custom seeds
- Updated GetToken() to properly use browser token for origin-specific noise

This is an Electron-specific feature for fingerprinting protection that differs
from Chromium's privacy model. Upstreaming is not planned.

